          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "epoca is a learned word usually traced to Greek epokhḗ \"a pause, a fixed point in time\", taken in through Medieval Latin (EtymDB has no Italian entry)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
